Constants:

- ES2015 introduces const to declare… constants!
- When you declare a variable with const, it has to be initialized and you can’t assign another
    value later.

🔦
you can initialize a constant with an object and later modify the object content. But you can't
assign another object.

        const PONY = {};    // declare and initialize empty object(PONY)
        PONY.color = 'blue';    // modify the object content ✅ works

        const PONY = {}; 
        PONY = {color: 'blue'};    // assign another object ❌ TypeError: Assignment to constant variable.

Same with the Array:

        const PC = [];  // declare and initialize empty Array(PC)
        PC.push('Monitor'); // modify the array content ✅ works
        PC.push({price: '70000'});  // modify the array content ✅ works

        const PC = [];  
        PC = [];    // ❌ TypeError: Assignment to constant variable.


